  "caption": "Coach Quinn's under-12s played three teams every weekend. When Pip had a sore spot near the knee for three weeks, Quinn said \"just growing pains\".\n\nKay explains that kids have growth plates near their joints, which are weaker than the nearby bone and tendon. Ongoing bone pain near a joint is worth checking.\n\nWhat can help: reduce training volume rather than stopping completely, keep strength work going, watch year-round single-sport schedules and multiple teams, adjust load during growth spurts, and remember supervised strength training is safe for kids. Don't play through bone pain.\n\nGet it checked after bone pain following a fall, pain lasting more than one to two weeks or getting worse, or a limp.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
